! ======================================================================
! test_v097_h2o_pbe_rij_optfreq -- RI-J analytical gradient:
! optimization + semi-numerical frequencies on the FITTED surface.
!
! Water PBE/6-31G(d), %ri j (def2-universal-JFIT).
!
! Reference (v0.97.0, 1 thread, reference BLAS):
!   Final energy:  -76.327908968223   (4 optimizer steps)
!   Modes:  1660.79 / 3614.86 / 3746.18 cm^-1
! Conventional opt+freq on the same route (%hess_method numerical):
!   -76.327810167189; 1661.15 / 3615.68 / 3747.25 cm^-1
!   -> fitted-vs-exact surface: dE = -99 uHa (33 uHa/atom),
!      frequencies within 0.4-1.1 cm^-1 (the standard J-fitting
!      class).  The analytic RI gradient matches central FD of the
!      RI energies to 5e-8 (O) / 1.2e-7 (H) au; UKS to 2.8e-7.
! The fitting tensor is rebuilt at every displaced geometry (PCM-
! cavity pattern); a staleness guard error-stops loudly otherwise.
! ======================================================================
%method  PBE
%basis   6-31gd
%job     opt+freq
%ri      j
%charge  0
%mult    1
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
